          "body": "Former England lock David Ribbans becomes eligible to represent South Africa on 27 October, when his three-year stand-down period ends. The 31-year-old Toulon forward won 11 caps for England, the last against Argentina in the 2023 World Cup third-place playoff. Rassie Erasmus has confirmed his interest in the Somerset West-born lock, but Ribbans has said he would not switch lightly, arguing that doing so would not be right towards England."
