          "body": "Exeter lock Dafydd Jenkins believes the steady stream of Wales players heading to English clubs will benefit the game at home. Jenkins, 23, pointed to Jac Morgan and Dewi Lake's summer moves from the Ospreys to Gloucester, arguing that Premiership competition improves players and opens places for younger hookers and back-rowers in the URC regions. Jenkins himself missed Wales's July Nations Championship games against South Africa, Argentina and Fiji after a shoulder operation, but has started all three of Exeter's league matches this season."
